<svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M2 4h12M2 8h12M2 12h8"></path></svg>
<span>Contents</span>
</button>

<div class="main">
<header class="intro">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="crumbs"><a href="/ko-mono-20">ko-mono-20</a> / User guide</nav>
<h1><span class="nowrap">ko-mono-20</span> user guide</h1>
<p class="lede">ko-mono-20 is the Korg MS-20, its whole circuit from the service manual, so its controls, patch panel and ESP work as the unit's do and the owner's manual applies. This guide covers what the plugin adds. Installing is on the <a href="/download#installing">download page</a>, and the ROM folder, artwork files, the update check and contact are on <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
<ol class="toc">
{toc.map(({ id, title }) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}
</ol>
</header>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="start">
<div class="eyebrow">1</div>
<h2>Getting started</h2>

<h3 id="first-start">The first start</h3>
<p>ko-mono-20 is a circuit with no firmware, so it needs no ROM. A new instance starts as a unit that's been on a while, with no cables in and the Rev 1 filter board. It plays without cables, because the patch panel's inputs are wired to their usual sources until you plug something in, as on the unit.</p>

<h3 id="artwork">Panel artwork</h3>
<p>The blank place for the KORG logo, bottom right, takes an SVG or PNG of your own, named as below, anywhere in the ROM folder (<a href="/support#artwork">how artwork files work</a>). <span class="k">ROMs</span> in the top bar shows whether it found one. There's no model name on the front of an MS-20.</p>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">File</th><th scope="col">Place</th><th scope="col">Size</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td class="mono">ko-mono-20-maker.svg or .png</td><td>The KORG logo, bottom right</td><td>39.0 × 12.3 mm</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>The plain name <span class="mono">maker.svg</span> in <span class="path">artwork/ms20/</span> works too.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="panel">
<div class="eyebrow">2</div>
<h2>The panel</h2>
<p>The MS-20's front panel, measured from photos. Everything on it works as on the unit except PHONES.</p>
<img src="/media/ko-mono-20/panel.png" alt="The panel with no cables in it" width="2732" height="1426" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">

<h3 id="sections">Its sections</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">VCO 1, VCO 2, the VCO MIXER and FREQUENCY MODULATION</span> - the two oscillators, their levels and how far the MG and EG 1 move their pitch, with PORTAMENTO and MASTER TUNE under them.</li>
<li><span class="k">The filters</span> - the HPF and the LPF, each with its CUTOFF FREQUENCY, PEAK and two modulation amounts.</li>
<li><span class="k">MODULATION GENERATOR, EG 1 and EG 2</span> - the MG and the two envelopes, with EG 2 on the VCA.</li>
<li><span class="k">The patch panel</span> - 35 jacks and VOLUME (see <a href="#patch">The patch panel</a>).</li>
<li><span class="k">EXTERNAL SIGNAL PROCESSOR</span> - the ESP, which turns an audio input into a pitch CV, an envelope and a trigger.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="patch">The patch panel</h3>
<p>Drag from one jack to another to patch a cable, an output into an input. One output can feed several inputs, and a cable in an input takes over from what's wired there, as on the unit. Drag a plug out of an input to move or pull its cable, or right-click a jack to pull all its cables. The bottom bar counts the cables.</p>

<h3 id="keys">The keyboard and the wheel</h3>
<p>The 37 keys run from C3 to C6, so at 8' a key sounds at its MIDI pitch. Like the unit's resistor ladder, the keyboard plays the highest key held, and legato never retriggers the envelopes.</p>
<p>The control wheel stays where you leave it, and the session saves it. The momentary switch under it is held down with the mouse or the <span class="k">1</span> key.</p>

<h3 id="power">POWER OFF</h3>
<p>VOLUME's counter-clockwise click is POWER OFF, as on the unit. Turn VOLUME up out of it and the MS-20 starts from cold, with its capacitors charging and EG 2 firing once, which makes a thump (quiet at the low VOLUME the switch leaves). Turn it back into the click and the sound dies with the power rails.</p>
<p>Opening a session or a new instance isn't a power-on, so ko-mono-20 starts settled, as if it had been on a while.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="bars">
<div class="eyebrow">3</div>
<h2>The bars</h2>

<h3 id="top-bar">The top bar</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">BETA</span> - this version is a beta, and About shows the version.</li>
<li><span class="k">ROMs</span> - the ROM folder and the <a href="#artwork">artwork</a>, with their full paths, and Show, Change… and Rescan for the folder.</li>
<li><span class="k">State</span> - see <a href="#state">State</a>.</li>
<li><span class="k">About</span> - the version, the ROM folder and artwork in use, the <a href="/support#updates">update check</a>, and links to this guide, the site and the forum. A newer version shows as a button in the bar.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="state">State</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">Save to file…</span> - saves the instance, with the knobs and switches, the cables, the wheel, the filter board and whether it's switched on.</li>
<li><span class="k">Load from file…</span> - loads one.</li>
<li><span class="k">Reset…</span> - makes it a new instance, as at the <a href="#first-start">first start</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="bottom-bar">The bottom bar</h3>
<dl class="legend">
<div><dt>SERVICE</dt><dd>Opens the service card, with CIRCUIT (<a href="#service">SERVICE</a>).</dd></div>
<div><dt>Status</dt><dd>How many cables are in, which jack has your DAW's audio, and the computer keys' octave (OCT). While keys are latched it shows those instead, and while the unit is off, POWER OFF.</dd></div>
<div><dt>?</dt><dd>Shows the list of computer keys over the panel. Any click, ? or Escape closes it.</dd></div>
</dl>

<h3 id="service">SERVICE</h3>
<p>CIRCUIT picks the filter board, as a unit has one or the other. <span class="k">REV 1</span> is the two KORG35 modules the service manual draws, and <span class="k">REV 2</span> is the later KLM-307, with LM13600 filters and its own VCA. Switching restarts the circuit settled, and the session keeps the board.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="daw">
<div class="eyebrow">4</div>
<h2>MIDI and your DAW</h2>

<h3 id="midi">MIDI</h3>
<p>The MS-20 has no MIDI, so the plugin plays its keys from MIDI notes. C3 to C6 play the 37 keys, and notes outside that fold in by octaves. Pitch bend moves the control wheel.</p>

<h3 id="audio-in">Audio in</h3>
<p>Route a track to the plugin's side-chain and it becomes a cable from outside. Click EXT SIGNAL IN to plug it in there, into the filters, or ESP SIGNAL IN to send it through the ESP, and click again to pull it out. The bottom bar says where it is, and whether your DAW has the input switched off.</p>

<h3 id="automation">Automation and sessions</h3>
<p>Every knob and switch on the panel can be automated. A session saves the instance as <a href="#state">State</a> does, and reopened, it carries on settled where it was, with the same cables and filter board.</p>
<p>When it has gone quiet the circuit sleeps, and the output is exact zeros. ko-mono-20 reports a 40 s tail.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="keyboard">
<div class="eyebrow">5</div>
<h2>Keyboard and mouse</h2>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">Knobs</span> - drag up or down, with Shift for fine steps, or scroll. Double-click for the start position.</li>
<li><span class="k">Rotary switches</span> - click for the next position, Shift-click or right-click for the one before, or drag round to one.</li>
<li><span class="k">Keys</span> - click, or slide along them to play them in turn. A right-click holds a key down until you click it again.</li>
<li><span class="k">The wheel</span> - drag up or down, and double-click to centre it.</li>
<li><span class="k">A W S E D F T G Y H U J K O L P ; '</span> - the keys from C4 (at OCT 0). <span class="k">Z, X</span> - octave down and up, -1 to +1. <span class="k">1</span> - the momentary switch.</li>
<li><span class="k">?</span> - shows the key list. <span class="k">Escape</span> closes it, lets go of held keys and drops a cable being drawn. Click the panel first, and Space goes to your DAW.</li>
<li><span class="k">Window</span> - drag the bottom-right corner.</li>
</ul>
</section>

</div>

</div>
</div>

</Base>

<script>
// The sidebar marks the heading being read and opens its section; the button opens it as a
// drawer on a narrow window. Without this script the sidebar shows every heading.
const nav = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.side')!;
const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.toc-button')!;
const links = [...nav.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a')];
const targets = links.map((a) => document.getElementById(a.hash.slice(1))!);
nav.classList.add('spy');
button.hidden = false;

let current = -1;
function mark() {
  let i = -1;
  targets.forEach((t, j) => { if (t.getBoundingClientRect().top <= 120) i = j; });
  // At the end of the page the last headings can't reach the top: take the one jumped to, if
  // it's in view, or else the last.
  if (innerHeight + scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 2) {
    const jumped = targets.findIndex((t) => '#' + t.id === location.hash);
    i = jumped >= 0 && targets[jumped].getBoundingClientRect().top < innerHeight ? jumped : targets.length - 1;
  }
  if (i === current) return;
  current = i;
  links.forEach((a, j) => {
    a.classList.toggle('on', j === i);
    if (j === i) a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'location'); else a.removeAttribute('aria-current');
  });
  const section = i >= 0 ? links[i].closest('.side > ol > li') : null;
  for (const li of nav.querySelectorAll(':scope > ol > li')) li.classList.toggle('open', li === section);
  reveal();
}

// Keep the marked heading in view when the sidebar is taller than the window.
function reveal() {
  const a = links[current];
  if (!a || nav.scrollHeight <= nav.clientHeight) return;
  if (a.offsetTop < nav.scrollTop || a.offsetTop + a.offsetHeight > nav.scrollTop + nav.clientHeight)
    nav.scrollTop = a.offsetTop - nav.clientHeight / 3;
}

let frame = 0;
const later = () => { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(() => { frame = 0; mark(); }); };
addEventListener('scroll', later, { passive: true });
addEventListener('resize', later);
addEventListener('hashchange', later);
mark();

function open(on: boolean) {
  nav.classList.toggle('open', on);
  button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(on));
  button.querySelector('span')!.textContent = on ? 'Close' : 'Contents';
  if (on) reveal();
}
button.addEventListener('click', () => open(!nav.classList.contains('open')));
nav.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if ((e.target as Element).closest('a')) open(false); });
document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  if (nav.classList.contains('open') && !nav.contains(e.target as Node) && !button.contains(e.target as Node)) open(false);
});
document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if (e.key === 'Escape' && nav.classList.contains('open')) { open(false); button.focus(); }
});
</script>

